00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:21.070
- There are multiple sides
of Schwab's business.

00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:23.280
And one of those sides
is the advisor side

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:24.600
or the institutional side.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:27.540
And obviously, we offer a lot of
products and a lot of services

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:28.980
to our institutional customers.

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:31.860
I'm responsible for making
sure that we deliver on behalf

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:32.950
of what our clients need.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.690
As we were looking
for solutions,

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:36.810
bringing about a
device to the branches

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:39.450
where, again, clients could
very easily open up an account,

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:41.770
we reached out to our
colleagues over at Google.

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:44.220
And we asked them whether
or not Google's Chromebook

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:46.380
was something that would
be applicable to what

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.485
we were trying to solve.

00:06:47.485 --> 00:06:48.360
That was on a Friday.

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:52.740
On Monday morning, we had two
of their top engineers engaged

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:54.690
with my engineers here.

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:56.979
3 and 1/2 hours later, I
get a knock on my door.

00:06:56.979 --> 00:06:58.770
And I'll never forget
what they said to me.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:00.450
They said, we've solved it.

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:03.870
Google offered a number of
services and capabilities

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:05.550
within their Chromebook
platform that

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:07.020
were incredibly attractive.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:10.950
One of them was the ability to
remotely control the devices.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.780
We could force them onto a
specific network, our network.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:16.030
If they fell off that network,
they would be unusable.

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:17.760
If someone stole them,
we had the ability

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:19.080
to remotely wipe them.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:20.880
I would say, one of the unique
features of the Chromebook

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:22.480
has to do with their
operating system.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:24.510
The device isn't burdened
with a lot of legacy

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:25.880
or with a large OS.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:28.590
Instead, the experience is,
you open the Chromebook.

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:30.240
And 10 seconds
later, you're online.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:32.640
Because of the kiosk capability
that the Chromebook had

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:34.470
to offer, when
one of our clients

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:36.584
came in to open
up a SIP account,

00:07:36.584 --> 00:07:37.750
we'd start up a new session.

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:40.590
And as soon as that Chromebook
was closed, session gone.

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:41.580
Everything gets erased.

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:44.370
The full rollout and development
started with a number

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:46.270
of weeks of user engagement.

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:48.830
We would take the Chromebooks
out to specific branches,

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:49.454
test it out.

00:07:49.454 --> 00:07:51.120
And then, from there,
it was making sure

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:53.620
that the device could stand up
and do exactly what we needed

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:55.270
it to do, but do it at scale.

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:57.390
When you're working with a firm
that's got hundreds of branches

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:59.556
out there and you're going
to eventually deploy well

00:07:59.556 --> 00:08:01.560
over 1,000 of these
devices, the ability

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:03.990
to control them from
a central location

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:05.100
is absolutely paramount.

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:07.990
And really, the Chromebook was
the one that met our needs.

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:10.603
They work at any
time, all the time.

00:08:10.603 --> 00:08:13.068
[END PLAYBACK]

